# Fleet session pitfalls (Web / App / Mobile)

Lessons from agent session workflows. Follow these to avoid repeat failures.

## Scripts & paths

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|--------|
| `npm run build:all-embeds` | `npm run build:embed:games` or `node scripts/games/build-all-embeds.mjs` |
| Assume `parallel-cli` on PATH | Check `which parallel-cli`; fall back to standard scripts |
| Edit only host `public/games/` | Fix upstream in source repo, then rebuild + vendor |

## Hub iframes

Lobby roots only: `/games/<slug>/` — never hub `iframeSrc` `/play`, `/campaign`, `/rush/*` (loads parent host SPA). See `hub-iframe-lobby-roots.mdc`.

- Playtest **embeds**: `npx serve public -l 4177` (game shells under `/games/<slug>/`).
- Playtest **hub `#games/<slug>` iframes**: `npx serve dist -l 4178` (or Vite preview) — `serve public` has no React `GamesSection`, so iframe `src` is always null.
- Touch: Header Restart must be `min-h/min-w` ≥44 — `px-3 py-1.5` alone fails the floor.
- **Wrong-slug false P0:** display-name URLs (`/games/mygame/`) are **not** embed folders. Cloudflare SPA fallthrough returns the host hub HTML. Canonicals already ship `index.html`. Host aliases live in `GAME_SPA_ALIASES`.
- Navigation mode tiles are `<a href>` (TanStack `Link`) — keyboard-tabbable. “0 buttons” is not an a11y P0; do not force `role="button"` onto navigation links.
- **Quick wins regression:** Theme labels without emoji; Restart SVG + 44px; CSR titles ≠ hub; display-name aliases.

## Android launchers

- Use clean, hyper-literal brand marks for launcher icons.
- Fallback: `scripts/games/android/assets/fleet-default-playstore-icon.png`.
- Per-game icons: install into `android/app/src/main/playstore-icon.png` then `resize-launcher-icons.mjs` (or [EasyAppIcon](https://easyappicon.com/) pack — never AppIcon.co / MakeAppIcon).
- `fix-icons.mjs` only fills **missing** mipmaps — wrong icons stay until replaced.

## Shared templates / sync

- Edit `scripts/games/templates/` then `sync-embed-ui.mjs` / `sync-win-overlay.mjs`.
- **Never** overwrite custom game-specific WinOverlays: keep `SKIP_WIN_OVERLAY` for titles with custom next labels / best UX.
- After sync, re-run tests that assert game-specific overlay strings.

## Contrast & chrome

- `--txt-lo` must stay ≥ ~4.5:1 on `--bg` / `--surface` (never `#4a4a4a` on `#0a0a0a`).
- Do not use `var(--btn-pri-bg)` (often a **gradient**) as CSS `color` for text — use `--txt-hi` / `--pp-accent` / `--pp-gold`.
- Canvas HUD under GameDock: raise engine Y / dock clearance — lobby `padding-bottom` does **not** shrink full-bleed canvas.

## Tests & e2e

- Assert visible copy users see (`/Cleared/i`), not only aria-label prose (`Level cleared`).
- After adding redirects, do not `doesNotMatch` all `navigate({ to: "/rush/$mode" })` — scope to Again/Home CTAs.
- Update structural tests when intentional class changes (e.g. `bottom-4` → `bottom-28` for dock clearance).

## Ship / vendor

1. Commit source repository **before** final vendor so `VENDOR-MANIFEST` `sha` == `git rev-parse HEAD`.
2. Docs-only commits after vendor → re-run vendor script or pin drifts.
3. Push: `main` then `main:master` when workflow uses both branches.
4. Use release scripts for rebuild+test+push without full manual game-tester audit.

## Do not commit

- `.DS_Store`, `*.code-workspace` junk, local keystores, secrets.
